# E1: exactness, arm 1. The gate's matrix plan on c2-packed-tp4-gate (slide ON, every audit on): four real-text users at 512 / 1,536
# / 4,096 / 16,384 tokens (the first two stay in the draft-history ramp for their whole answer, the others are at the steady state),
# 256 tokens out, a concurrent arm (packed-4 rounds) and a solo arm (the same prompts one at a time), strict policy: every
# concurrent text must equal its solo text. The prompts are the image's own real-text corpus by (user index, length), so E2 and E3
# serve the SAME four prompts.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card speed window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/speed and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image K0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_GATE_JIT=record: the growth of the kernel cache is recorded, not judged (no four-card warm plan exists).
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; per arm an engine build 5-15 min plus 3-8 min of streams: 20 / 35 / 100 min.
# Read: the gate verdict per arm; per user IDENTICAL concurrent against solo; the audits clean (extent, T1, T2); zero refusals; the
# [ACCEPT] line; the divergence records file if any user differs.
# STOP on FAIL, NOT_COMPARABLE, UNSTABLE or an audit mismatch.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-speed-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
C2_GATE_PLAN=matrix
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=512,1536,4096,16384
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=256
C2_GATE_JIT=record
